WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:06.710
Hello everyone, and welcome to this session on Twinmotion to Unreal Engine.

2
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:10.609
My name is Amer Yassine and I will be your guide today.

3
00:00:10.609 --> 00:00:14.250
The purpose of this class is to show you how to export your Twinmotion project to

4
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.699
Unreal Engine for further processing.

5
00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:22.260
We'll cover the recommended workflows, as well as tips and tricks to ensure the best

6
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.399
compatibility between the two apps.

7
00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:29.519
You'll first learn about setting the stage, and what plugins you need to help with the

8
00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:31.500
transfer.

9
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.579
You'll then learn to ingest the Twinmotion data into Unreal Engine in a couple of different

10
00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:41.920
ways, before you learn to manage lights, levels of detail and collisions.

11
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:48.380
Finally, you will learn how to fix or replace those effects that didn't transfer properly.

12
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:56.219
We'll be using Twinmotion Community Edition 2023.2 and Unreal Engine 5.3 for this class.

13
00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:58.780
And so, if you're ready, let's start!
